(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRuleApply", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"9ee72faf-0ffa-f94b-820b-70616fd54e8e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRuleApply", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "hg"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ae63dbd8-0b8d-374d-a779-f81415835cc1"],
 " ",
 "applies rule to the hypergraph hg, giving a list of events, one for every \
way the rule's input matches."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"ad8f3db3-3abb-ce49-be94-4ace4dbca487"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"97394f35-33b0-c14e-a405-111a621d2a32"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"7329e5ed-e73c-e948-a871-3fefe117a4db"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"7b17a2fa-ba03-4741-adea-be77713443eb"],

Cell["\<\
Each event is an association. \"Hypergraph\" is the result; \
\"MatchVertices\", \"MatchEdges\" and \"MatchEdgePositions\" say what was \
matched; \"NewVertices\" and \"NewEdges\" what was created; \"DeletedVertices\
\" what was destroyed; \"RuleVertexMap\" the correspondence from the rule's \
vertices to the hypergraph's; and \"Rule\" the rule itself.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3431b4c7-175a-4c43-8f88-2f8a8c0df627"],

Cell["\<\
The result is the hypergraph with the matched edges removed and the output's \
edges put in their place. A vertex the output introduces becomes a new vertex \
of the result, and one the output drops is destroyed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"42d7deb0-6699-2043-8b53-2c6785692e16"],

Cell["\<\
A destroyed vertex is removed only when nothing still standing uses it. A \
rule rewrites what it matched, and reaching into edges it did not match to \
strike a vertex out of them would not be local; so a vertex the rule drops \
but another edge still holds simply stays, and is not reported destroyed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f902423-fd97-7541-95d4-68f16fd2ef1f"],

Cell["\<\
New vertices are named so as to miss every vertex already present, which \
makes the result reproducible from one session to the next rather than \
depending on a counter of fresh symbols.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f9561f1-7a74-e946-bf14-8e8cd2270c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A label on the input is read three ways. A bare symbol is a **variable**: \
it matches whatever label it is laid against and remembers it, and every \
later occurrence of that symbol must find the same thing. No label at all is \
a wildcard, matching anything and remembering nothing. Anything else \
\[LongDash] a string, a number, a composite expression \[LongDash] is a \
literal and matches only itself; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Verbatim", "[", "x", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"03985e46-cc5f-b84d-985f-25d3d5d751a0"],
 " forces a symbol to be read that way too."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c78ac445-94c4-0f48-9c86-d75d033f6ad8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output's labels are expressions in those variables, written out with \
the bindings substituted. A rule may therefore name what it builds after what \
it found, which is how a pair of composable edges labelled x and y becomes \
one labelled for their composite. The bindings are reported with the event as \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<LabelBindings\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9521c5e5-6f6d-d647-8b37-3c37d1eb2b05"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5a7784b3-46ea-1240-bd74-3fef81d9e927"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels bind in the same way as edge labels, so a rule whose whole \
input is one labelled vertex binds that label and may name what it creates \
after it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ac84a0bf-619e-9149-aa0c-a3d164ff5645"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"84731359-d3b5-c644-a772-ee3a9424e9f0"],
 " ignores labels altogether; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<LabelPatterns\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5aeab7f8-95fe-cc4b-a80a-2ce32cb0da7e"],
 " keeps labels significant but reads every one of them literally, symbols \
included."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"13406eb2-a529-2e4d-a0ca-4139c80c4e49"],

Cell["\<\
Where the output gives a vertex a label, that label is the one the result \
carries: relabelling is something a rule is entitled to do. Where the output \
leaves a vertex unlabelled, whatever the hypergraph had is kept.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3d0620fa-a16e-9a48-829a-d6defcf6e526"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types must agree, and the pattern is matched over the orderings its \
symmetry allows: one for a directed edge, its rotations for a cyclic one, \
every permutation for an unordered one. An unordered edge of arity k \
therefore matches in k! ways, which are genuinely different matches and are \
all reported.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"30188d86-3b84-e745-98c7-35cca78f895c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<DistinctVertices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa5edde8-562c-b14a-86b4-e78405aaa222"],
 ", the default, keeps two vertices of the input from landing on one vertex \
of the hypergraph, which is what the reference paclet does. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["False", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0a9d2f90-e5fc-a94c-9406-20b3d3a41cd0"],
 " allows it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"39c1395a-1a68-1445-a01e-3352d61b0941"],

Cell["\<\
No match gives an empty list, which is not a failure: it says the rule does \
not apply.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3cf94cd7-4376-414f-a4ab-480d66110cbe"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"cc654678-d328-fd42-8a6d-a5738cf46c49"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge of a two-edge path: one event for each edge.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"aa8f6bf1-73f8-3546-be79-9d56bd30f99d"],

Cell["\<\
sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}];
chain = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}], Edge[{2, 3}]}];
events = sub[chain];
Length[events]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0440418f-e946-1a41-950e-5f6655b37821"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"62bcdc6f-6235-0940-923c-e0c014616412"],

Cell["What the first event did:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ec06a16f-ce3d-c34c-9cea-7e75ec4aea29"],

Cell["\<\
KeyTake[First[events], {\"MatchEdgePositions\", \"NewVertices\", \
\"RuleVertexMap\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5ddfd13-38b9-6741-b547-af53ab6665ff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"MatchEdgePositions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"NewVertices\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[FormalV]", "[", "1", "]"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"RuleVertexMap\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"\[FormalV]", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}],
   "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b8177ba1-d225-9547-\
9ff9-9d47c970bbb8"],

Cell["And what it produced:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"7a064556-6ad3-ba4f-8b9b-4675922cde0d"],

Cell["First[events][\"Hypergraph\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1d5b5d20-95b4-7341-8b58-046189ab78e6"],

